      "text": "I've designed the CourtPass mobile landing page, focusing on a clean, high-performance aesthetic that highlights the Sheikh Zayed courts.\n\n### Key Design Decisions:\n- **Visual Hierarchy**: The hero section uses your professional court photography (Professional, high-quality photograph of a modern outdoor padel court with blue turf and glass walls, located in a clean architectural setting in Sheikh Zayed, Egypt. Bright daylight, luxury sports club feel. Used as a background image with a light green overlay.) as a high-impact backdrop for the \"Book. Pay. Play.\" value proposition, immediately followed by a high-visibility CTA.\n- **Brand Consistency**: I've applied the primary #1B7A4E green for the main actions and branding, while using the #E86A2A orange specifically for the \"Morning Promo\" card to create a distinct visual \"early bird\" cue.\n- **Information Architecture**: The \"How it Works\" and \"Today at a Glance\" sections use card-based layouts to break down information into digestible, mobile-friendly chunks, ensuring users can see court availability at a glance.\n- **Light & Airy Feel**: The #F4F7F5 background provides a soft contrast to the crisp white cards, maintaining a premium \"sports club\" feel that aligns with the photography.\n\nThe design is fully responsive for a 390px mobile viewport and strictly follows your Light Mode requirements."
